   * opened by tapping a Notifee notification from a quit state.
   * Stores the pending room ID so Splash can consume it after session restore.
   */
  public static checkInitialNotification = async () => {
    const initialNotification = await notifee.getInitialNotification();
    if (initialNotification) {
      await this.handleNotificationPress(initialNotification.notification, true);
    }
  };

  /** Get and clear the pending room navigation (used by Splash screen) */
  public static consumePendingRoomId = (): string | null => {
    const roomId = this.pendingRoomId;
    this.pendingRoomId = null;
    return roomId;
  };

  public static setPendingRoomId = (roomId: string) => {
    this.pendingRoomId = roomId;
  };

  private static handleNotificationPress = async (
    notification: Notification | undefined,
    isInitialNotification: boolean,
  ) => {
    const roomId = notification?.data?.room_id;

    if (!roomId || typeof roomId !== "string") return;

    // For initial notification (cold start), store the room_id
    // and let the Splash screen handle navigation after session restoration
    if (isInitialNotification) {
      this.pendingRoomId = roomId;
      return;
    }

    // Refresh the room list before navigating to ensure it's up to date
    await MatrixCore.refreshRoomList();
    await MatrixCore.getClient().awaitRoomRemoteEcho(roomId);

    // For foreground/background events (app already running), navigate directly to room
    NavigationContainerRef.navigate("room", { roomId });
  };

  public static create = (payload: CreatePayload) =>
    notifee.displayNotification({
      android: {
        pressAction: { id: "default" },
        channelId: this.channelId,
        autoCancel: true,
        color: "#292929",
      },
      title: payload.title,
      body: payload.message,
      id: payload.id,
      data: payload.data,
    });
}

content.text:
Looking at the cold-start flow carefully:

1. App killed → FCM arrives → background handler creates Notifee notification
2. User taps → cold start → Splash runs
3. Splash calls `NotifeeService.checkInitialNotification()` → `consumePendingRoomId()`

The `isCurrentlyViewingRoom` check itself **shouldn't break cold start** — when nav isn't ready, it returns `false` at line 68, so notifications aren't suppressed. But there's a real race condition that might have surfaced at the same time.

In `registerListeners` ([PushNotificationsService.ts:251](src/modules/push-notifications/service/PushNotificationsService.ts#L251)):
```js
getInitialNotification(getMessaging()).then((remoteMessage) => {
  handleNotificationPress(remoteMessage, true);  // calls setPendingRoomId
});
```

This `.then()` is **not awaited**. The order in Splash ([Splash.tsx:92-95](src/screens/splash/Splash.tsx#L92-L95)):

```js
await NotifeeService.checkInitialNotification();  // sets pendingRoomId via Notifee
const pendingRoomId = NotifeeService.consumePendingRoomId();
```

`consumePendingRoomId` can be called **before** the Firebase `.then()` resolves. If the user tapped a **Notifee** local notification (not the raw Firebase one), Firebase's `getInitialNotification` returns `null` — so only the Notifee path matters. If `notifee.getInitialNotification()` returns `null` for any reason (e.g., the background FCM handler failed to create the notification silently), `pendingRoomId` stays `null` → Splash goes to home.

The most likely root cause: when the app is killed and an **encrypted** message arrives, `ensureServiceInitialized()` ([line 113](src/modules/push-notifications/service/PushNotificationsService.ts#L113)) may fail or the decryption throws, so `NotifeeService.create` is never called. No Notifee notification is created. What the user taps is a **raw Firebase notification** (if the FCM payload has a `notification` field). Firebase's `getInitialNotification` picks it up — but by the time `.then()` resolves, `consumePendingRoomId` has already been called.

**Concrete fix** — await the Firebase initial notification before consuming in Splash, or add a fallback in `PushNotificationsService` to handle the case where the Notifee path produces nothing. Add logging first to confirm:

```ts
public static checkInitialNotification = async () => {
  const initialNotification = await notifee.getInitialNotification();
  console.log("[Notifee] initial notification:", initialNotification?.notification?.data);
  if (initialNotification) {
    await this.handleNotificationPress(initialNotification.notification, true);
  }
};
```

And in Splash, add a log after `consumePendingRoomId` to see if it's null. That will tell you whether the issue is Notifee not finding the initial notification, or something else further up in the background handler.

